{
  "accountSummary": "Probook is an AI operating system for home services, built around dispatch to unify intake, data cleaning, chat, outbound, and dispatch. It sells to US home-services contractors in plumbing, HVAC, and electrical, serving a fragmented SMB market. Probook is at the Series A stage with 52 employees, 14 open positions listed, and a stated plan to scale go-to-market, engineering, and customer success. It is on this list for review because its Series A funding and expanding GTM hiring align with the Series A vertical-AI project.",
  "whyNow": [
    {
      "headline": "Series A funding creates a GTM and delivery expansion window",
      "quote": "a16z is leading Probook’s $34 million Series A",
      "sourceDomain": "a16z.com"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Probook is scaling GTM, engineering, and customer success for demand",
      "quote": "Probook says it will \"scale its go-to-market team against surging demand, and grow engineering and customer success to deliver on it.\"",
      "sourceDomain": "www.globenewswire.com"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Six open GTM roles signal active customer acquisition investment",
      "quote": "We have a clearly defined target: the top home service operators in America. The list exists. The product is proven. What we need now is someone to go get them.",
      "sourceDomain": "jobs.ashbyhq.com"
    },
    {
      "headline": "The GTM stack lacks CRM, sales engagement, data, and ABM tools",
      "quote": "current_technologies (30 detected): no CRM, no sales-engagement tool, no data provider and no ABM/intent platform are present; LinkedIn Ads and LinkedIn Recruiter are the only GTM tools detected",
      "sourceDomain": "apollo.io"
    }
  ],
